# apps/collector — ingest.
#
# LEAVE UNUSED VARIABLES COMMENTED OUT, never blank — see the note at the top of
# api.env.example.
#
# This is the internet-facing service, and its FORBIDDEN list is the longest in
# the system: it exits at startup if handed any ClickHouse credential, any
# Stripe key, AUTH_SECRET, QUERY_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY,
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, an OAuth client secret, the object-storage key pair,
# OA_CREDENTIAL_KEYRING or OPENAI_API_KEY. Its whole job is to validate and
# enqueue.

NODE_ENV=production
ENVIRONMENT=production
LOG_LEVEL=info
PORT=8083

# Read-only, for the per-site ingest config, cached with a short versioned TTL.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://openanalytics:{{POSTGRES_PASSWORD}}@postgres:5432/openanalytics
# Postgres on Neon (recommended managed option — ../NEON.md): the DIRECT
# connection string, pooling off, so no `-pooler` in the host. The same string
# goes in api.env, collector.env, worker.env and migrate.env.
#DATABASE_URL=postgresql://neondb_owner:<password>@ep-example-123456.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&channel_binding=require

# BOTH VALKEY URLS ARE ADDRESSED BY IP, NOT BY SERVICE NAME. The connection
# factory refuses a plaintext redis:// URL whose host is not provably private,
# because this hop can hold the only copy of a customer event — and a compose
# service name is not a private host as far as that check is concerned. See
# note 2 in docker-compose.yml.
EVENT_STREAM_REDIS_URL=redis://:{{VALKEY_QUEUE_PASSWORD}}@{{VALKEY_QUEUE_IP}}:6379
REALTIME_CACHE_REDIS_URL=redis://:{{VALKEY_REALTIME_PASSWORD}}@{{VALKEY_REALTIME_IP}}:6379

# The anonymous-identity HMAC. THIS SERVICE IS THE ONLY ONE THAT EVER SEES A RAW
# VISITOR IP: the address is turned into a daily-rotating hash here and then
# discarded, and no field downstream can hold one.
#
# The worker needs the SAME value, byte for byte, for revenue attribution —
# `./generate-secrets.sh` writes one value into both files. A different value
# there does not fail; it joins against nothing while looking exactly like a
# value that should.
ANONYMOUS_IDENTITY_SECRET={{ANONYMOUS_IDENTITY_SECRET}}
ANONYMOUS_IDENTITY_KEY_VERSION=1

# City-level geolocation, resolved locally — no lookup leaves this host. Point
# this at a City-schema .mmdb in `infra/selfhost/geoip/`, which the compose file
# mounts at /geoip read-only. UNSET, EVERY EVENT CARRIES NULL GEO — a
# degradation, never a failure, and the reason a fresh install shows every
# country as unknown.
#
# `cd geoip && ./fetch-dbip.sh` downloads DB-IP City Lite (CC BY 4.0: no
# account, redistributable with attribution). A MaxMind GeoLite2-City.mmdb works
# just as well if you already have one — the schemas are interchangeable.
# GEOIP_DB_PATH=/geoip/dbip-city-lite.mmdb

# METRICS_REMOTE_WRITE_URL=
# METRICS_REMOTE_WRITE_USER=
# METRICS_REMOTE_WRITE_TOKEN=
